{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>The entire congregation.</b> All of them whole and standing to enter the Land — for there was not among them a single one of those upon whom the decree had been pronounced, since the dead of the wilderness had already all perished, and these are of those about whom is written concerning them ״חַיִּים כֻּלְּכֶם הַיּוֹם״ (Deuteronomy 4) (Tanchuma)." "<b>Mount Hor.</b> A mountain upon a mountain, like a small apple atop a large apple. And even though the cloud went before them and leveled the mountains, three remained in them — Mount Sinai for the Torah, and Mount Hor for the burial of Aharon, and Mount Nevo for the burial of Moshe (Tanchuma)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:11:47.039496545Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}